	// decides whether a verdict exists at all is whether a block can be named. Read the
	// chain successfully and the answer is attestable even when it is not terminal, which
	// is why `outcome` carries `undetermined` alongside the two terminal values: the
	// verifier looked, at a named final block, and the window is still open. Fail to read
	// the chain and there is no block to anchor anything to, so no verdict is issued and
	// the case goes out unsigned through the root `error` as `VERIFICATION_ERROR`. A
	// consumer MUST NOT treat either of those as terminal: the payment stays pending and is
	// re-asked. NEITHER a client polling budget expiring, NOR an HTTP 5xx, NOR a network
	// error is a finding about the payment either, and a consumer MUST NOT derive one from
	// any of them.
